{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788369687,"nonce":"yxKUYRY7bSkftzZcz04j5bvSBwA=","message":"**Bench evidence, orchestrator, 2026-09-02. Held `state:doing` — the detection half is proven, one acceptance clause is BROKEN in shipped code.**\n\nPlaced `templates/bedroom.ir.json` at [138,142] on a live map (`ly-1`, preflight 22 checked / 0 failed), then read it:\n\n```\n$ rwa construction --layout_id ly-1  -\u003e  data.enclosure\n  intends_room      : true          declared_rooms : 1\n  shell_cells       : 20            interior_cells : 15\n  enclosed          : true          \u003c- ProperRoom: the walls closed\n  uses_outdoor_temp : true          \u003c- THE SECOND MECHANISM\n  open_shell_cells  : 0             shell_complete : true\n  unroofed_cells    : 15\n  unroofed          : [[139,143],[140,143],[141,143],[139,144],…]   (every cell named)\n```\n\n**This is exactly the case the acceptance was widened for.** A sealed room — shell complete, `ProperRoom` true — that is nonetheless on outdoor temperature because it has no roof. A check reporting only `enclosed` would have passed this clean, and that is the freezer.\n\n\nAcceptance item 2 asks the report to **name the gap**. It does not:\n\n```\n\"gaps\": \"System.Collections.Generic.List`1[System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]]\"\n```\n\nA .NET type name, consistently, in both the gapless and the populated case. Root-caused: `MiniJson.cs:75` matches `case List\u003cobject\u003e` — that exact closed type — while `PlaceVerbs.cs:1177` declares `List\u003cDictionary\u003cstring, object\u003e\u003e Gaps` and `:1215` puts it straight into the envelope. It matches no case, hits the default, and is `ToString()`'d. No throw, no warning. `first_gap` at `:1264` is a single `Dictionary` and serializes correctly, so a caller reading `first_gap` sees the right thing while `gaps` beside it is garbage.\n\nFiled separately as **`4950f14` (p1)**, with the scope checked rather than assumed: of eight declarations of that type in the mod, `PlaceVerbs.cs:1215` is the only one reaching an envelope directly. `DesignateReach.cs:458` hand-converts around the same trap (`new List\u003cobject\u003e(v.Unreadable.ToArray())`), which is the clearest evidence it is a trap worth closing.\n\n\n- Enclosure detection: **proven**, both mechanisms, distinctly.\n- Roof reporting: **proven**, names every unroofed cell.\n- \"Name the gap\": **broken**, tracked at `4950f14`.\n\n\nThe round's acceptance asks to *leave one wall cell unbuilt and be told the room is not enclosed*. I proved the roof half of that shape, not the wall half — I did not remove a shell cell and observe `enclosed` flip to false with the open cell named, because `gaps` is unreadable regardless until `4950f14` lands. `rooms.layouts_unenclosed` and `digest.construction.layouts_unenclosed` were also not read on a bench.","files":null}]}